WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.345
Lesson 14.1.

00:00:02.345 --> 00:00:05.894
Monitoring: dashboards, alerts and on-chain watchers.

00:00:05.894 --> 00:00:07.821
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:07.821 --> 00:00:09.800
able to set up monitoring so you hear

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.779
about problems before they cost money.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.369
Here's the plan.

00:00:14.369 --> 00:00:16.054
First, the key ideas.

00:00:16.054 --> 00:00:18.769
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:18.769 --> 00:00:20.294
Then, your checklist.

00:00:20.294 --> 00:00:22.456
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:29.857
Watch four things: Tools: portfolio dashboards, protocol-native alerts, wallet-activity

00:00:29.857 --> 00:00:35.149
watchers, block-explorer address alerts, and official status/X accounts.

00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:36.864
Alerts should reach your phone.

00:00:36.864 --> 00:00:40.556
First, Positions: health factors, LP ranges, pegs,

00:00:40.556 --> 00:00:43.389
utilisation of markets you lend to.

00:00:43.389 --> 00:00:48.762
Next, Protocols: governance proposals, queued upgrades (timelocks), incidents.

00:00:48.762 --> 00:00:51.685
Then, Wallets: any outgoing transaction or

00:00:51.685 --> 00:00:55.179
new approval from your vault/operating wallets.

00:00:55.179 --> 00:00:59.211
And finally, Market: funding, large depegs, liquidations.

00:01:00.512 --> 00:01:03.520
HF, credit line, < 2.0 /

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:06.467
< 1.7, Repay per 11.3.

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:10.647
Stablecoin peg, < 0.99 for 2h, Peg rule.

00:01:10.647 --> 00:01:13.450
Market utilisation, > 95% for

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:16.367
24h, Withdraw per kill rule.

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:20.870
Vault wallet outflow, Any, Verify immediately (11.5).

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:23.225
Queued upgrade, Any, on protocols >

00:01:23.225 --> 00:01:25.580
10% of book, Review within timelock.

00:01:26.879 --> 00:01:28.339
Here's your checklist.

00:01:28.339 --> 00:01:29.874
Do it now, for real.

00:01:29.874 --> 00:01:33.769
First, Alerts for all four categories, delivered to phone.

00:01:33.769 --> 00:01:36.664
And finally, every alert maps to a written action.

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:39.174
Question 1.

00:01:39.174 --> 00:01:41.289
Why alert on any vault-wallet outflow?

00:01:45.709 --> 00:01:48.062
The answer: The vault should almost never

00:01:48.062 --> 00:01:50.359
move; any movement could be a compromise.

00:01:51.659 --> 00:01:52.904
Question 2.

00:01:52.904 --> 00:01:54.379
Why watch queued upgrades?

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:01.141
The answer: The timelock is your window

00:02:01.141 --> 00:02:03.424
to exit before the change takes effect.

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:05.994
Question 3. An

00:02:05.994 --> 00:02:08.139
alert with no action attached is…?

00:02:13.394 --> 00:02:15.129
The answer: Noise. Every

00:02:15.129 --> 00:02:17.214
alert needs a written response.

00:02:18.514 --> 00:02:19.759
Let's recap.

00:02:19.759 --> 00:02:23.023
Positions: health factors, LP ranges, pegs,

00:02:23.023 --> 00:02:25.919
utilisation of markets you lend to.

00:02:25.919 --> 00:02:30.794
Protocols: governance proposals, queued upgrades (timelocks), incidents.

00:02:30.794 --> 00:02:33.504
Wallets: any outgoing transaction or new

00:02:33.504 --> 00:02:36.647
approval from your vault/operating wallets.

00:02:36.647 --> 00:02:39.868
Market: funding, large depegs, liquidations.

00:02:41.169 --> 00:02:43.684
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:43.684 --> 00:02:47.335
Next up, Lesson 14.2: Automation: keepers, bots

00:02:47.335 --> 00:02:50.453
and agents without handing over the keys.
